# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the pyion C-layer concurrency test.
#
# CPython 3.13's free-threading mode is experimental, and ThreadSanitizer
# reports data races inside the interpreter itself -- biased reference
# counting (Python/brc.c), dict internals (Objects/dictobject.c), and so on.
# Those are CPython issues, not pyion issues.
#
# These suppressions scope the TSan run to pyion's own C code: a race whose
# offending accesses originate inside libpython is suppressed, so the run
# fails only on a race in pyion's C extension (base_bp.c, _bp.c, _mgmt.c, ...).
called_from_lib:libpython3.13t.so
